# Normalize line endings; Go sources are LF in the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Compiled SPIR-V is committed on purpose: shaders/shaders.go embeds it with
# go:embed, so without these files the module does not build for anyone who
# `go get`s it. glslc is therefore an authoring-only dependency.
*.spv binary

# Binary assets. Deliberately NOT tracked with Git LFS -- the Go module proxy
# does not run LFS smudge, so consumers would receive pointer stubs where
# go:embed and the asset loaders expect real content.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.glb  binary
*.bin  binary
*.wav  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.heightmap binary

# ── GitHub language stats (Linguist) ──
#
# miniaudio is a vendored single-header C library, and at ~4 MB it is six times
# the size of all the Go in this repository. Linguist counts bytes, so without
# this the project is reported as a C project. `vendored` is the accurate
# label: it is third-party code we redistribute but do not maintain.
audio/miniaudio.c linguist-vendored
audio/miniaudio.h linguist-vendored

# Compiled SPIR-V is a build artifact of the .vert/.frag sources beside it,
# committed only so `go get` works. It is not hand-written source.
*.spv linguist-generated

# Shared GLSL includes; Linguist otherwise guesses from the .inc extension.
shaders/*.inc linguist-language=GLSL
